<div class="mk-crumbbar"><div class="mk-wrap in"><a href="#">Markets</a><span class="sep">&rsaquo;</span><a href="/markets/industrial-iot">Industrial &amp; IoT</a><span class="sep">&rsaquo;</span><span class="here">RFID Asset Tracking</span></div></div><div class="mk-spoke-grid"><aside class="mk-side"><div class="side-head"><span class="side-head-label">Industrial &amp; IoT products</span><button type="button" class="mk-side-toggle" aria-label="Collapse sidebar"><span class="chev"><i data-lucide="chevron-right" style="width:13px;height:13px;"></i></span></button></div><a class="s" href="/markets/industrial-iot/pcba-box-build"><span class="abbr">PB</span><span class="label">PCBA &amp; Box Build</span></a><a class="s" href="/markets/industrial-iot/iot-device-assembly"><span class="abbr">ID</span><span class="label">IoT Device Assembly</span></a><a class="s active" href="/markets/industrial-iot/rfid-asset-tracking"><span class="abbr">RT</span><span class="label">RFID Asset Tracking</span></a><a class="s" href="/markets/industrial-iot/power-modules"><span class="abbr">PM</span><span class="label">Power Modules</span></a><div class="helper"><div class="h">Not sure which fits?</div><p>Tell us what the product does and where it runs and we&rsquo;ll point you to the right line.</p><a class="cta" href="/contact">Work with us <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></a></div></aside><div class="mk-spoke-main"><section class="mk-hero" data-hana-bg="flow" data-variant="light" data-fade="none"><div class="mk-wrap mk-hero-in"><div><div class="mk-eyebrow">Industrial &amp; IoT &middot; RFID Asset Tracking</div><h1 class="mk-h1">RFID tags for industrial asset tracking</h1><p class="mk-lede">An industrial asset tag is a construction problem, not a printing one. It gets fixed to metal, knocked by tools and pallets, washed down and left outdoors — and it still has to read cleanly on a forklift pass or through a dock door.</p><div class="mk-btns"><a href="/contact" class="hana-btn hana-btn-primary" style="padding:12px 22px;font-size:12px;">Talk to us <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:14px;height:14px;margin-left:6px;"></i></a><a href="#specialize-rfid-asset-tracking" class="hana-btn hana-btn-secondary" style="padding:12px 22px;font-size:12px;">What we specialize in</a></div></div><div class="mk-hero-media"><div class="mk-ph" style="aspect-ratio:auto;height:420px;border-bottom:0;"><div style="position:absolute;top:10px;left:12px;width:18px;height:18px;opacity:.4;z-index:1;"><svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--hana-blue)" stroke-width="1.5"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"></circle><path d="M12 3v4M12 17v4M3 12h4M17 12h4"></path></svg></div><span class="cap">[ RFID Asset Tracking &mdash; photography needed ]</span></div></div></div></section><section id="specialize-rfid-asset-tracking" data-hana-bg="hex" data-variant="light" data-fade="none" style="background:var(--bg);border-top:1px solid var(--line);position:relative;overflow:hidden;"><div class="mk-wrap" style="position:relative;z-index:1;padding-top:64px;padding-bottom:60px;"><div style="max-width:700px;margin-bottom:26px;"><h2 class="mk-h2">What we specialize in</h2><p class="mk-body">Hana builds tags for that: hardened and rubber-embeddable formats, on-metal constructions that keep a UHF antenna working against a metal surface, and temperature-sensing tags where a program needs one. Underneath them are inlays and straps off roll-to-roll automated lines, six of them at our Jiaxing plant. Hana has manufactured and designed RFID products for more than twenty years.</p></div><div class="mk-sheet"><div class="row"><div class="lab"><span class="n">01</span><span class="t">Rugged and on-metal UHF tags</span></div><div class="desc">hardened tag constructions for mounting on equipment and on metal, with the format chosen for the mounting surface.</div></div><div class="row"><div class="lab"><span class="n">02</span><span class="t">UHF inlays and straps</span></div><div class="desc">the inlay and strap layer underneath, built on roll-to-roll automated lines.</div></div><div class="row"><div class="lab"><span class="n">03</span><span class="t">Rubber-embeddable and temperature-sensing formats</span></div><div class="desc">embeddable constructions and temperature-sensing tags where the application calls for them.</div></div><div class="row"><div class="lab"><span class="n">04</span><span class="t">Encoding, unique ID and read verification</span></div><div class="desc">a unique identity per tag, with read performance verified on the finished tag as part of the build.</div></div></div><div class="mk-caplinks"><p class="note">Process depth sits on the capability page: RFID Inlay owns the antenna and converting processes underneath every tag construction, including the tuning work a difficult mounting surface demands.</p><div class="links"><a href="/capabilities/rfid-smart-tags/rfid-inlays">Explore RFID Inlay <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></a></div></div></div></section><section class="mk-dark"><div class="mk-wrap in"><div style="max-width:820px;"><h2 class="mk-h2 on-dark">Ruggedization and read range</h2><p class="mk-body on-dark" style="margin:0 0 14px;">Two things decide whether an industrial tag is any good: what it is built to withstand, and how far it reads once it is mounted. Hana treats both as build questions. The construction — materials, encapsulation, antenna design and the standoff that lets a UHF antenna work close to metal — is chosen for the mounting surface and the handling the tag will see, not fitted afterwards. Read performance is then verified on the built tag rather than inferred from the inlay. Hana's UHF tags are certified under the ARC (Auburn) program in the USA and China, which puts read performance in front of an independent test house rather than an internal one.</p></div></div></section><section style="background:var(--hana-blue-tint);border-top:1px solid var(--line);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);"><div class="mk-wrap" style="padding-top:56px;padding-bottom:56px;"><div style="max-width:700px;margin-bottom:24px;"><div class="mk-eyebrow">Footprint</div><h2 class="mk-h2 sm">Where we build</h2></div><div class="mk-locs"><a class="mk-loc" href="/locations/jiaxing"><span class="co"><i data-lucide="map-pin" style="width:13px;height:13px;color:var(--hana-blue);"></i><span class="hana-spec-label">China</span></span><div class="nm">Jiaxing</div><div class="note">automated RFID inlay lines</div><span class="cta">View plant <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></span></a><a class="mk-loc" href="/locations/ohio"><span class="co"><i data-lucide="map-pin" style="width:13px;height:13px;color:var(--hana-blue);"></i><span class="hana-spec-label">USA</span></span><div class="nm">Ohio</div><div class="note">UHF inlays, straps and ruggedized tags</div><span class="cta">View plant <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:12px;height:12px;"></i></span></a></div><p style="margin:18px 0 0;"><a href="/locations" class="hana-link" style="font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.1em;">All locations <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:13px;height:13px;"></i></a></p></div></section><section style="background:#fff;border-top:1px solid var(--line);"><div class="mk-wrap" style="padding-top:56px;padding-bottom:60px;"><div style="max-width:700px;margin-bottom:22px;"><div class="mk-eyebrow">FAQ</div><h2 class="mk-h2 sm">Frequently asked questions</h2></div><div style="max-width:860px;"><details class="mk-faq" open><summary><span class="mk-faq-mk"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span><span style="flex:1;">What makes an industrial RFID tag different from a label?</span></summary><p class="mk-faq-a">Construction. An adhesive label carries an inlay and little else. An industrial tag is a built assembly — encapsulated, with materials and an antenna design chosen for the mounting surface and the handling it will see, including on-metal constructions that keep a UHF antenna readable against metal.</p></details><details class="mk-faq"><summary><span class="mk-faq-mk"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span><span style="flex:1;">What read range can industrial UHF tags achieve?</span></summary><p class="mk-faq-a">Range depends on the tag construction, the mounting surface and the reader set-up, so it is settled per program rather than quoted as one figure. What Hana can do is verify read performance on the built tag — and our UHF tags are certified under the ARC (Auburn) program in the USA and China, where range is measured independently.</p></details><details class="mk-faq"><summary><span class="mk-faq-mk"><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span><span style="flex:1;">Does Hana have experience manufacturing RFID at volume?</span></summary><p class="mk-faq-a">Yes. Hana has manufactured and designed RFID products for more than twenty years, on roll-to-roll automated inlay lines — six at Jiaxing — with inlay and strap production also running in Ohio.</p></details></div><div style="margin-top:40px;padding-top:26px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);"><a href="/markets/industrial-iot" class="hana-link" style="font-size:11px;letter-spacing:0.1em;"><i data-lucide="arrow-left" style="width:13px;height:13px;"></i> Back to the Industrial &amp; IoT market hub</a></div></div></section><section class="mk-cta" data-hana-bg="flow" data-variant="dark" data-fade="none"><div class="mk-wrap in"><div><h2 class="mk-h2 on-dark" style="max-width:520px;">Talk to us about your asset-tracking program</h2><p class="mk-body on-dark" style="font-size:16px;max-width:480px;">Tell us what you need built and we will come back with a plan.</p></div><div class="acts"><a href="/contact" class="hana-btn hana-btn-on-dark" style="padding:12px 22px;font-size:12px;">Contact us <i data-lucide="arrow-right" style="width:14px;height:14px;margin-left:6px;"></i></a></div></div></section></div></div>
